# Reverse raw readiness and radio audit — 20261113T123510Z

- Purpose: distinguish an absent RF header from a software/capture event loss.
- Hypothesis: previous readiness lacked an operational register snapshot; add observations without changing the PHY to locate the failing boundary.
- Initial state: both boards in verified normal unarmed standby, proof `20261113T121735Z-standby`; operator antenna/915 MHz authorization remains in force.
- Source revision: `1e2dd303e2ca63b93826df030e8fd116683d7284`, dirty source identities preserved in `.automation/ack-investigation/mission-baseline/source-hashes.json`; exact candidates copied before programming.
- One changed experimental variable: diagnostic instrumentation and stricter evidence gating. Frequency, power (2 dBm PA_BOOST), SF7/BW125/CR4/5, sync 0x12, explicit header, CRC and normal IQ unchanged. No timing/bit-3/power experiments bundled.
- Expected: active RX continuous before exactly one 11-byte Tracker transmission; counters and IRQ captured before read/cleanup, then verified normal standby restoration.
- Command authorized for this experiment: `uv run python tools/arq_trial.py --reverse-raw --rf-path-confirmed`.
- Hardware: Rudolph serial `42032240221023150129012600000000`, Tracker `42032240221092150158013400000000`; signature `1e970a`, fuses `0000f0ffffd2f80000ffffffffffffff`; existing bounded writer rechecks identities, ranges and protected memory before/after each application write.
- Firmware hashes, actual results, evidence and verdict: [bounded attempt 20261113T123620Z](20261113T123620Z.md). No RF success claimed.

## Repository and prior evidence

Active ARQ V1 is `src/arq/main.cpp`, with codec/state machines under `src/arq/`.
Raw reverse is isolated in `src/reverse_raw/main.cpp`; original `src/mvp/main.cpp` remains unchanged.
`/home/parinya/university/iwing-tracker/gateway-lora/loraboard` is a legacy related gateway application using the project LoRa wrapper/task framework (its `lora_rx.cpp` declares 440 MHz/20 dBm). It is not the active ARQ V1 image; none of those legacy settings are imported.

Previous bundle `20261113T121506Z-reverse-raw`: all 62 original hashes reverified.
Host monotonic RX command: `102247558567569`; RX_READY received: `102248120085196`;
SEND issued: `102248120149471`; TX_DONE received: `102249775309902`.
RX_READY precedes SEND by 64,275 ns at the host. Cross-MCU uptimes were not compared.
Both monitors were already acquired to establish identities before arming RX; starting another UPDI monitor after RX_READY would add unnecessary receive-window delay.
The existing runner already had a readiness barrier. Its limitation was missing active mode evidence and a host 15-second wait that could expire before the mailbox delivered the actual 15-second device timeout. The old final drained stream contains that timeout and is a valid negative RF observation.

New host barrier requires RX_READY rc=0, LoRa RX-continuous mode with the shared-register page clear, an audited active RX profile and a host elapsed bound under 10 seconds from RX command to SEND. Device RX remains 15 seconds; only the host drain allowance is 20 seconds. No handshake or retry was added.

## Driver and IRQ audit

Installed RadioLib is 7.1.2. Real public-HAL tests confirm begin/carrier E4C000,
IRQ reads without clears, W1C flags, TX FIFO and mode, finishTransmit 833 us/standby,
RX Continuous, readData clearing IRQ even on CRC error, and unchanged modem/IQ configuration across TX/RX.
SX127x has no finishReceive method. Firmware polls actual IRQ registers, so DIO0 wiring is recorded but an ISR is not required. Repeated RX commands are rejected without rearming or clearing an event. RxDone is snapshotted before standby/readData; packet handling precedes deadline handling.

Configuration snapshot address order:
`42 01 06 07 08 09 4D 1D 1E 26 20 21 39 33 3B 11 40 41 0C 31 37 24 4B`.
RAW_CONFIG is standby, RAW_TX_PRE is immediately before startTransmit, RAW_TX_STATE follows startTransmit, RAW_RX_ACTIVE follows startReceive.
Observations contain flags, header/packet counters, mode, ModemStat, HopChannel and accumulated observed flags. Header observation is bounded to one event; at most two packet observations, using the existing sixteen-slot nonblocking logger. Overflow invalidates evidence. No periodic log stream or repeated initialization was introduced.

[Semtech SX1276 datasheet, pp.106–111](https://cdn.sparkfun.com/assets/7/7/3/2/2/SX1276_Datasheet.pdf): bit 3 defaults to one and selects access to band-specific test registers. RadioLib setMode writes bits 2:0 and setFrequency writes the carrier; neither changes bit 3. Thus 0x89/8B/8D are explained by retained reset state. Source evidence does not establish a defective RF-band selection. No bit change is justified yet.
RegInvertIQ is handled deliberately by RadioLib invertIQ(false): RX bit6 clear, TX bit0 set, IQ2=1D. Its source documents swapped TX polarity relative to datasheet wording (issue778). Actual reserved bits produce 27; the zero-reserved-bit fake HAL produces01. Do not override this library behavior speculatively.
Counters 14–17 describe receive observations; Semtech specifies reset in Sleep and counts since transition into RX. Samples are taken in the same RX window before cleanup; fake HAL does not prove silicon counter lifetime.

## Software verification before RF

188 host tests run: OK, one obsolete BOOT repair class skipped. Seven reverse-raw host tests pass after focused changes; RED/GREEN outputs in `.automation/ack-investigation/`.
All six normal/test/reverse images built successfully. Real RadioLib HAL characterization passes. Generator check and diff whitespace checks pass.
Repository isolation and LoRa SSOT validation passed before programming.

